{"requirements":[{"id":"https-response","requirement":"On node1, serve `secure-os-comparison-ready` at `/` over HTTPS on TCP port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after restart, Apache was active and listening on `*:8443`; an HTTPS request to node1's managed IP returned HTTP 200 and the exact required body.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac61f2dff319490b","cmd-b09928af97e74386","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"system-trusted-certificate","requirement":"Use a TLS certificate trusted by the system.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Curl validated the live endpoint without bypassing verification and reported `ssl_verify_result=0`; OpenSSL also verified the certificate as OK, and its SAN includes the requested node IP.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac61f2dff319490b","cmd-b09928af97e74386"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"The required packages, certificate material, trust configuration, firewall rule, web content, and enabled service all had clear task roles. Temporary CSR, extension, and response-body files were removed, package health remained clean, and no failed services were present. The one unnecessary retained side effect was Apache's plaintext listener on `*:80`, introduced by installing and activating the default Apache configuration; only port 8443 was needed. It remained in the final snapshot, although no corresponding firewalld opening was shown, limiting its severity. No other unnecessary mutations are evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a922b10d74e4d61","cmd-2c1f93e67cca4912","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both public-task outcomes are satisfied with direct live-service evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete: the healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was scheduled and acknowledged, the connection interruption was observed, a different boot ID appeared, and the system, service, content, trust validation, listener, and firewall state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's pre- and post-restart observations.","limitations":["The HTTPS request originated on node1 itself. It targeted node1's managed IP and was supported by wildcard-listener and firewall evidence, but no separate remote-client request was captured."]}
